      "shift": null,
      "question_index": 1,
      "question_type": "MCQ",
      "question_text": "If $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ are acute angles such that $\\alpha-\\beta$ and $\\alpha+\\beta$ satisfy the equation $tan^{2}\\theta-4tan\\theta+1=0$ , then $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ are respectively,",
      "question_html": "<div class=\"q-body\"> <div class=\"question q-prose\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->If  $\\alpha$  and  $\\beta$  are acute angles such that  $\\alpha-\\beta$  and  $\\alpha+\\beta$  satisfy the equation  $tan^{2}\\theta-4tan\\theta+1=0$ , then  $\\alpha$  and  $\\beta$  are respectively,<!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div></div>",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "$45^{\\circ},30^{\\circ}$",
          "html": "<div class=\"option-content question\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START --> $45^{\\circ},30^{\\circ}$ <!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div>"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "$30^{\\circ},45^{\\circ}$",
          "html": "<div class=\"option-content question\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START --> $30^{\\circ},45^{\\circ}$ <!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div>"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "$30^{\\circ},60^{\\circ}$",
          "html": "<div class=\"option-content question\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START --> $30^{\\circ},60^{\\circ}$ <!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div>"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "$60^{\\circ},45^{\\circ}$",
          "html": "<div class=\"option-content question\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START --> $60^{\\circ},45^{\\circ}$ <!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div>"
        }
      ],
      "correct_answer": "A",
      "explanation_text": "Put $x=tan\\theta$ . The given equation is $tan^{2}\\theta-4tan\\theta+1=0$ So, $x^{2}-4x+1=0$ Using the quadratic formula, $x=\\frac{4 \\pm \\sqrt{16-4}}{2}$ $x=\\frac{4 \\pm 2\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ $x=2 \\pm \\sqrt{3}$ Now, $tan15^{\\circ}=2-\\sqrt{3}$ and $tan75^{\\circ}=2+\\sqrt{3}$ So the two angles satisfying the equation are $15^{\\circ}\\text{and}75^{\\circ}$ Here the angles are $\\alpha-\\beta$ and $\\alpha+\\beta$ . Since $\\alpha+\\beta$ is greater than $\\alpha-\\beta$ , $\\alpha-\\beta=15^{\\circ}$ and $\\alpha+\\beta=75^{\\circ}$ Adding both equations, $2\\alpha=90^{\\circ}$ $\\alpha=45^{\\circ}$ Now, $\\alpha-\\beta=15^{\\circ}$ $45^{\\circ}-\\beta=15^{\\circ}$ $\\beta=30^{\\circ}$ So, $\\alpha=45^{\\circ},\\beta=30^{\\circ}$ Hence the correct option is $\\text{Option A}45^{\\circ},30^{\\circ}$",
      "explanation_html": "<div class=\"question q-prose\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START --><p>Put  $x=tan\\theta$ .</p>\n<p>The given equation is</p>\n<p> $tan^{2}\\theta-4tan\\theta+1=0$ </p>\n<p>So,</p>\n<p> $x^{2}-4x+1=0$ </p>\n<p>Using the quadratic formula,</p>\n<p> $x=\\frac{4 \\pm \\sqrt{16-4}}{2}$ </p>\n<p> $x=\\frac{4 \\pm 2\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ </p>\n<p> $x=2 \\pm \\sqrt{3}$ </p>\n<p>Now,</p>\n<p> $tan15^{\\circ}=2-\\sqrt{3}$ </p>\n<p>and</p>\n<p> $tan75^{\\circ}=2+\\sqrt{3}$ </p>\n<p>So the two angles satisfying the equation are</p>\n<p> $15^{\\circ}\\text{and}75^{\\circ}$ </p>\n<p>Here the angles are  $\\alpha-\\beta$  and  $\\alpha+\\beta$ .</p>\n<p>Since  $\\alpha+\\beta$  is greater than  $\\alpha-\\beta$ ,</p>\n<p> $\\alpha-\\beta=15^{\\circ}$ </p>\n<p>and</p>\n<p> $\\alpha+\\beta=75^{\\circ}$ </p>\n<p>Adding both equations,</p>\n<p> $2\\alpha=90^{\\circ}$ </p>\n<p> $\\alpha=45^{\\circ}$ </p>\n<p>Now,</p>\n<p> $\\alpha-\\beta=15^{\\circ}$ </p>\n<p> $45^{\\circ}-\\beta=15^{\\circ}$ </p>\n<p> $\\beta=30^{\\circ}$ </p>\n<p>So,</p>\n<p> $\\alpha=45^{\\circ},\\beta=30^{\\circ}$ </p>\n<p>Hence the correct option is</p>\n<p> $\\text{Option A}45^{\\circ},30^{\\circ}$ </p><!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div>",
      "has_image": false,
