        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{12}$",
          "html": "<div class=\"option-content question\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START --> $\\frac{\\pi}{12}$ <!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div>"
        }
      ],
      "correct_answer": "D",
      "explanation_text": "Let $y=x+\\frac{\\pi}{6}$ Then the expression becomes $siny+cosy$ We know that $siny+cosy=\\sqrt{2}sin(y+\\frac{\\pi}{4})$ The maximum value of $sin(y+\\frac{\\pi}{4})$ is $1$ . So the maximum value is attained when $y+\\frac{\\pi}{4}=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ This gives $y=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$ Now substitute back: $x+\\frac{\\pi}{6}=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$ $x=\\frac{\\pi}{4}-\\frac{\\pi}{6}$ $x=\\frac{3\\pi-2\\pi}{12}$ $x=\\frac{\\pi}{12}$ So the correct option is $\\frac{\\pi}{12}$ Option D.",
      "explanation_html": "<div class=\"question q-prose\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START --><p>Let</p>\n<p> $y=x+\\frac{\\pi}{6}$ </p>\n<p>Then the expression becomes</p>\n<p> $siny+cosy$ </p>\n<p>We know that</p>\n<p> $siny+cosy=\\sqrt{2}sin(y+\\frac{\\pi}{4})$ </p>\n<p>The maximum value of  $sin(y+\\frac{\\pi}{4})$  is  $1$ .</p>\n<p>So the maximum value is attained when</p>\n<p> $y+\\frac{\\pi}{4}=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ </p>\n<p>This gives</p>\n<p> $y=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$ </p>\n<p>Now substitute back:</p>\n<p> $x+\\frac{\\pi}{6}=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$ </p>\n<p> $x=\\frac{\\pi}{4}-\\frac{\\pi}{6}$ </p>\n<p> $x=\\frac{3\\pi-2\\pi}{12}$ </p>\n<p> $x=\\frac{\\pi}{12}$ </p>\n<p>So the correct option is</p>\n<p> $\\frac{\\pi}{12}$ </p>\n<p>Option D.</p><!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div>",
