      "correct_answer": null,
      "explanation_text": "To find the minimum value of the expression $f(x)=1-sinx$ , we start by considering the range of the sine function. Since $-1 \\le sinx \\le 1$ , this means the minimum value of $sinx$ is $-1$ . Now, compute $f(x)$ when $sinx=-1$ : $f(x)=1-(-1)=1+1=2$ Check if $sinx=1$ : $f(x)=1-1=0$ Thus, the minimum value of $f(x)=1-sinx$ occurs when $sinx=1$ , making the minimum value: $f_{min}=0$",
      "explanation_html": "<div class=\"question q-prose\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START --><p>To find the minimum value of the expression  $f(x)=1-sinx$ , we start by considering the range of the sine function. Since  $-1 \\le sinx \\le 1$ , this means the minimum value of  $sinx$  is  $-1$ .</p>\n<p>Now, compute  $f(x)$  when  $sinx=-1$ :</p>\n<p> $f(x)=1-(-1)=1+1=2$ </p>\n<p>Check if  $sinx=1$ :</p>\n<p> $f(x)=1-1=0$ </p>\n<p>Thus, the minimum value of  $f(x)=1-sinx$  occurs when  $sinx=1$ , making the minimum value:</p>\n<p> $f_{min}=0$ </p><!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div>",
